e><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Nakagawa</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Dor&#x000e9;e</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Labb&#x000e9;</surname><given-names>J.-C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Nigg</surname><given-names>E.A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title><italic>In vitro</italic> disassembly of the nuclear lamina and M phase-specific phosphorylation of lamins by cd2 kinase</article-title><source>Cell.</source><volume>61</volume><year>1990</year><fpage>591</fpage><lpage>602</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2188731</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Pyrpasopoulouetal1996"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pyrpasopoulou</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Meier</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Maison</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Simos</surname><given-names>G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Georgatos</surname><given-names>S.D.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The lamin B receptor (LBR) provides essential chromatin docking sites at the nuclear envelope</article-title><source>EMBO (Eur. Mol. Biol. Organ.) J.</source><volume>15</volume><year>1996</year><fpage>7108</fpage><lpage>7119</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="Riabowoletal1988"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Riabowol</surname><given-names>K.T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Fink</surname><given-names>J.S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Gilman</surname><given-names>M.Z.</given-names></name><name><surname>Walsh</surname><given-names>D.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Goodman</surname><given-names>R.H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Feramisco</surname><given-names>J.R.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The catalytic subunit of cAMP-dependent protein kinase induces expression o